WEBVTT

00:00:16.592 --> 00:00:24.728
The Chideb presents The True Story of Pocahontas by Kelly Reinhart.

00:00:24.788 --> 00:00:38.835
Is this a true story?

00:00:38.895 --> 00:00:50.950
Yes, this is a true story.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:01:00.513
The Indian Princess, Pocahontas, was born near Jamestown in 1595.

00:01:00.573 --> 00:01:08.146
Captain John Smith wrote many of the events of this story in his books.

00:01:08.206 --> 00:01:14.568
Some details were added and other details were forgotten.

00:01:14.628 --> 00:01:20.520
But the story you will read in this book really happened.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.312
This is the true story of Pocahontas.

00:01:26.372 --> 00:01:39.696
Chapter 1 The Sailing Ship May was a beautiful month in the land of the Algonquin Indians.

00:01:39.756 --> 00:01:44.832
There were tall trees and colorful flowers everywhere.

00:01:44.892 --> 00:01:49.270
The sky and the sea were deep blue.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:56.464
Pocahontas was the favorite daughter of Chief Poe Hatton.

00:01:56.524 --> 00:01:59.716
She was an Indian princess.

00:01:59.776 --> 00:02:06.470
Chief Poe Hatton was a powerful chief of the Algonquin tribe.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.004
Pocahontas was 11 years old.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:18.110
She was a lovely young girl with black hair and dark eyes.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:22.812
She wore a buckskin dress and moccasins.

00:02:22.872 --> 00:02:26.634
She had a feather in her hair.

00:02:26.694 --> 00:02:30.668
Pocahontas was always happy.

00:02:30.728 --> 00:02:35.710
She ran in the forest and danced in the fields.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:40.942
She sat on the hill and looked at the blue sea.

00:02:41.002 --> 00:02:52.810
On May 6, 1607, Pocahontas sat on the hill and she saw something strange in the bay.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.433
It was a big sailing ship.

00:02:56.493 --> 00:03:00.026
She was very surprised.

00:03:00.086 --> 00:03:03.980
The sailing ship was something new.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.423
It had big white sails and flags.

00:03:08.483 --> 00:03:12.655
She looked at it for a long time.

00:03:12.715 --> 00:03:15.287
Where did it come from?

00:03:15.346 --> 00:03:17.818
Why was it there?

00:03:17.878 --> 00:03:21.150
She was very excited.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:27.824
Pocahontas ran to her village to tell her father and brother the news.

00:03:27.884 --> 00:03:29.725
Father, father.

00:03:29.785 --> 00:03:33.908
She said, there's a big sailing ship in the bay.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:38.312
It has white sails and coloured flags.

00:03:38.372 --> 00:03:44.787
Her father, Chief Powhatan, was outside his long house.

00:03:44.847 --> 00:03:49.320
He was a tall man with long black hair.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:54.264
He wore the feathers of an Indian chief on his head.

00:03:54.324 --> 00:03:59.448
He listened to the news, but he was not happy.

00:03:59.508 --> 00:04:04.301
The white men are here, Powhatan said sadly.

00:04:04.361 --> 00:04:07.210
This is bad news for our people.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:11.540
There is no peace with the white men here.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.742
Nantakwas was Pocahontas' brother.

00:04:15.802 --> 00:04:19.184
He was 18 years old.

00:04:19.245 --> 00:04:22.716
He was a strong Indian warrior.

00:04:22.776 --> 00:04:30.201
He looked at his sister and said, In the past, the white people killed the Indians.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.138
They want to take our land.

00:04:33.198 --> 00:04:37.887
Oh, Nantakos, let's go to see the white people.

00:04:37.947 --> 00:04:40.588
Let's go to see their big ship.

00:04:40.648 --> 00:04:43.420
Said Pocahontas.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:49.554
You can go to see them, but don't go near the ship.

00:04:49.614 --> 00:04:52.004
Stay far away.

00:04:52.064 --> 00:04:53.906
Be careful.

00:04:53.965 --> 00:04:56.346
Said Pocahontas.

00:04:56.406 --> 00:04:59.348
Remember Pocahontas.

00:04:59.408 --> 00:05:03.010
White men are dangerous.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:07.842
Nantakwas and Pocahontas went to the river.

00:05:07.902 --> 00:05:11.452
There were many canoes near the river.

00:05:11.512 --> 00:05:14.674
They got into a small canoe.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:20.336
Then Nantakwas paddled down the river to the bay.

00:05:20.396 --> 00:05:25.408
In the bay they saw the big sailing ship.

00:05:25.468 --> 00:05:29.619
There was a tall white man on the ship.

00:05:29.679 --> 00:05:32.093
He smiled at them.

00:05:32.153 --> 00:05:35.367
There were other white men, too.

00:05:35.427 --> 00:05:40.990
They all looked at the small canoe and at the two Indians.

00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:44.311
Pocahontas smiled at the white man.

00:05:44.371 --> 00:05:47.692
Let's go to the ship, she said.

00:05:47.752 --> 00:05:50.754
No, said Nantakwas.

00:05:50.814 --> 00:05:52.284
It's dangerous.

00:05:52.344 --> 00:05:55.706
We don't know who these white men are.

00:05:55.766 --> 00:05:58.597
We can look and then go home.

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:01.435
We must obey our father.

00:06:01.495 --> 00:06:05.334
The white man on the ship smiled again.

00:06:05.394 --> 00:06:07.116
Look, Nantakos.

00:06:07.176 --> 00:06:08.727
Said Pocahontas.

00:06:08.787 --> 00:06:13.060
That man has red hair and white skin.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.393
He's smiling at us.

00:06:15.452 --> 00:06:17.534
Look at his clothes.

00:06:17.594 --> 00:06:19.716
They are strange.

00:06:19.776 --> 00:06:24.730
Nantakos turned the canoe and paddled up the river.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:31.603
When they arrived home, Nantakos said, I saw a big sailing ship.

00:06:31.663 --> 00:06:34.973
There were many white men on the ship.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:40.586
Powhatan talked to his medicine men and tribe advisors.

00:06:40.646 --> 00:06:45.800
They all sat inside the longhouse for a long time.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:50.864
He said, white men bring us problems.

00:06:50.924 --> 00:06:53.666
They have a strange magic.

00:06:53.726 --> 00:06:57.526
They carry thundersticks to kill our people.

00:06:57.586 --> 00:07:04.201
They want to take our land, our lakes, our rivers, and our forests.

00:07:04.261 --> 00:07:09.967
They can stay for a short time, but they cannot stay here forever.

00:07:10.027 --> 00:07:17.578
Let's watch them and see what they do.

