00:09:45.144 --> 00:10:27.058
Jurgen Heinrich, Chris Bruckner, Rob Klein, Iklaude Birkman, Iklaude Kursa, Orok Pirwe, Manahod himself Berdini, Virupartu, Inavagzale, Chris Bruckner, Priyegal Smundhina, Nadevavuevstrichu, Robert, Hochi Prostoposmatret Berlin, Klaudevstrichate, Ivognavagzale, Chapter 2 Pocahontas meets John Smith Captain John Smith and his men were happy to be in Chesapeake Bay.

00:10:27.118 --> 00:10:44.466
They wanted to establish a small settlement there.

00:10:44.526 --> 00:10:53.421
Captain Smith called the Big River the James River after King James I of Britain.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:11:02.656
On May 13, 1607, he established the small settlement called Jamestown.

00:11:02.716 --> 00:11:06.850
Jamestown was on the James River.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:15.244
In Jamestown, the settlers built some huts, a storehouse, and a church.

00:11:15.304 --> 00:11:22.348
There were about 100 men in Jamestown in 1607.

00:11:22.408 --> 00:11:26.348
Most of them were English gentlemen.

00:11:26.408 --> 00:11:32.050
They came to the new world to find gold and riches.

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:36.277
They did not want to be farmers.

00:11:36.337 --> 00:11:40.294
John Smith was angry with them.

00:11:40.353 --> 00:11:45.156
He said, you must all plant crops, hunt and fish.

00:11:45.216 --> 00:11:47.626
You must not be lazy.

00:11:47.686 --> 00:11:51.938
In Jamestown, there was little food.

00:11:51.998 --> 00:11:58.541
One day, Captain Smith and his men went into the forest to look for food.

00:11:58.601 --> 00:12:01.922
They walked for a long time.

00:12:01.982 --> 00:12:05.878
Then they met a big group of Indians.

00:12:05.938 --> 00:12:10.464
The Indians attacked them with their bows and arrows.

00:12:10.524 --> 00:12:13.936
They killed one of Smith's men.

00:12:13.996 --> 00:12:19.320
John Smith and his men killed two Indians.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:25.644
Then the Indians captured John Smith and took him away.

00:12:25.704 --> 00:12:35.233
After a long walk, John Smith stood in front of Chief Poehaten and his tribe.

00:12:35.293 --> 00:12:38.208
Everyone was silent.

00:12:38.268 --> 00:12:41.939
Pocahontas stood next to her father.

00:12:41.999 --> 00:12:44.730
She looked at John Smith.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:47.251
He was very tall.

00:12:47.311 --> 00:12:54.274
She looked at his red hair, his blue eyes, and his white skin.

00:12:54.334 --> 00:12:59.200
He was very different from the Indian men.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:07.092
John Smith spoke to the Indians in sign language and a few Indian words.

00:13:07.152 --> 00:13:10.294
Great Chief, I am a friend.

00:13:10.354 --> 00:13:14.228
My men and I want to live in peace with you.

00:13:14.288 --> 00:13:19.482
Powhatan and his medicine men did not like him.

00:13:19.542 --> 00:13:24.296
John Smith gave a compass to the great chief.

00:13:24.356 --> 00:13:27.190
Powhatan looked at it.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:31.006
He turned it around in his hand.

00:13:31.066 --> 00:13:36.370
Why did the needle always point in the same direction?

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:41.896
He tried to touch the needle, but a piece of ice was in front of it.

00:13:41.956 --> 00:13:44.348
The ice wasn't cold.

00:13:44.408 --> 00:13:46.370
It didn't melt.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.574
Pohaton thought it was magic.

00:13:49.634 --> 00:13:54.272
All the Indians of the tribe looked at the compass.

00:13:54.332 --> 00:13:58.980
They were surprised at the white man's magic.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:06.933
Pocahontas liked John Smith and his magic, but her father didn't like him.

00:14:06.993 --> 00:14:13.486
That afternoon, John Smith and his men killed two Indians.

00:14:13.546 --> 00:14:18.408
Chief Powhatan and his tribe were very angry.

00:14:18.468 --> 00:14:22.076
Now John Smith must die.

00:14:22.136 --> 00:14:27.714
Two Indian warriors pushed Captain Smith to the ground.

00:14:27.774 --> 00:14:31.996
They put his head on a very big stone.

00:14:32.055 --> 00:14:36.558
Then the Indians picked up another big stone.

00:14:36.618 --> 00:14:40.269
They wanted to kill John Smith.

00:14:40.329 --> 00:14:46.801
When Pocahontas saw this, she said, No father, please don't kill him.

00:14:46.861 --> 00:14:48.912
He isn't a bad man.

00:14:48.972 --> 00:14:55.390
Pohatan said, No, he and his men killed two Indians.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.592
He must die.

00:14:57.652 --> 00:15:02.476
The two Indians were ready to kill Captain Smith.

00:15:02.536 --> 00:15:05.177
One Indian raised his hand.

00:15:05.237 --> 00:15:06.028
No!

00:15:06.088 --> 00:15:07.759
said Pocahontas.

00:15:07.819 --> 00:15:13.152
She jumped forward and put her head above Captain Smith's head.

00:15:13.212 --> 00:15:15.974
Please, Father, he must not die.

00:15:16.034 --> 00:15:17.142
Save him.

00:15:17.202 --> 00:15:19.050
said Pocahontas.

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:23.244
Pohatan looked at his favorite daughter.

00:15:23.304 --> 00:15:27.628
He immediately told the two Indians to stop.

00:15:27.688 --> 00:15:32.492
Everyone was surprised at Pocahontas' courage.

00:15:32.552 --> 00:15:36.876
Pocahontas saved John Smith's life.

00:15:36.936 --> 00:15:43.310
After this, Pocahontas and John Smith became great friends.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:50.031
John Smith taught her English, and she taught him the Indian language.

00:15:50.092 --> 00:15:54.164
He gave her beautiful beads and trinkets.

00:15:54.224 --> 00:15:59.397
He told her about London and its enormous buildings.

00:15:59.457 --> 00:16:03.670
Pocahontas listened to Smith's stories.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:08.092
A King of England is called King James I.

00:16:08.152 --> 00:16:13.312
He lives in a beautiful palace in London, said John Smith.

00:16:13.372 --> 00:16:15.119
Is he your chief?

00:16:15.179 --> 00:16:17.360
Asked Pocahontas.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:20.121
Yes, he's our leader.

00:16:20.181 --> 00:16:22.032
Said John Smith.

00:16:22.092 --> 00:16:24.804
What do the English ladies wear?

00:16:24.863 --> 00:16:26.854
Asked Pocahontas.

00:16:26.914 --> 00:16:31.237
They wear long colorful dresses, shoes and hats.

00:16:31.297 --> 00:16:33.418
They also wear jewels.

00:16:33.478 --> 00:16:35.809
Are the English ladies beautiful?

00:16:35.869 --> 00:16:41.612
Pocahontas asked, some are beautiful and some aren't.

00:16:41.672 --> 00:16:43.901
Said John Smith.

00:16:43.961 --> 00:16:47.080
Pocahontas laughed and listened.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:17:02.380
She dreamt about London.

