00:18:40.708 --> 00:18:50.892
King James wanted his explorers to find gold, riches and food products in the new world.

00:18:50.952 --> 00:18:57.066
He also hoped to find a new way to go to India.

00:18:57.126 --> 00:19:03.910
Captain John Smith was one of the leaders of the Virginia Company.

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:07.251
He was a courageous soldier.

00:19:07.311 --> 00:19:12.891
When he was young, his life was full of adventure.

00:19:12.951 --> 00:19:18.052
He and the Austrians fought against the Turks.

00:19:18.113 --> 00:19:22.414
The Austrians were very pleased with him.

00:19:22.474 --> 00:19:31.386
They gave him a horse, a scimitar, a coat of arms, and the title of Captain.

00:19:31.446 --> 00:19:36.806
Then Captain Smith was captured by the Turks.

00:19:36.866 --> 00:19:41.579
He was a prisoner in Turkey, but he escaped.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:50.856
He crossed Russia, sailed on a pirate ship, and returned to England in 1604.

00:19:50.916 --> 00:19:55.900
Captain Smith then worked for the Virginia Company.

00:19:55.961 --> 00:20:00.074
He took the English settlers to the New World.

00:20:00.134 --> 00:20:03.953
He was a strong, intelligent leader.

00:20:04.013 --> 00:20:07.962
He established the settlement of Jamestown.

00:20:08.022 --> 00:20:13.326
He explored the Chesapeake region and made maps.

00:20:13.386 --> 00:20:19.068
He made friends with many Indian tribes in the region.

00:20:19.128 --> 00:20:28.222
The settlers did not find gold and riches in the new colony, but they found the tobacco plant.

00:20:28.282 --> 00:20:35.392
In the 17th century, the tobacco plant grew only in America.

00:20:35.452 --> 00:20:40.374
The American Indians smoked the tobacco leaves.

00:20:40.434 --> 00:20:44.556
They used the leaves as medicine too.

00:20:44.616 --> 00:20:51.178
The tobacco plant became the most important product of the Virginia colony.

00:20:51.238 --> 00:20:57.036
There were many tobacco plantations along the James River.

00:20:57.096 --> 00:21:01.206
The tobacco leaves were picked and dried.

00:21:01.266 --> 00:21:06.170
Then they were sent to England and other parts of Europe.

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:11.075
This was the beginning of an important business.

00:21:11.135 --> 00:21:15.439
Soon there were tobacco companies everywhere.

00:21:15.499 --> 00:21:22.881
With its tobacco plantations, Virginia became a very rich colony.

00:21:22.941 --> 00:21:30.770
By 1688, it produced about 10 million kilograms of tobacco.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:43.553
Smoking became very popular in America and Europe.

00:21:43.613 --> 00:21:53.835
My name is Brokna.

00:21:53.895 --> 00:21:57.828
My family is Brokna.

00:21:57.868 --> 00:22:00.230
My family is Brokna.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:13.292
My family is Brokna.

00:22:13.352 --> 00:22:24.422
Hello, Rob.

00:22:24.482 --> 00:22:25.852
Hello, Claudia.

00:22:25.912 --> 00:22:28.824
Privetrop, Privet, Claudia.

00:22:28.884 --> 00:22:30.756
Vigetstya.

00:22:30.817 --> 00:22:32.538
Kajla.

00:22:32.598 --> 00:22:34.659
Danke, Gutt.

00:22:34.719 --> 00:22:37.761
Khrashou, Spasiba.

00:22:37.821 --> 00:22:40.784
Chapter 3.

00:22:40.844 --> 00:22:44.436
Winter in Jamestown.

00:22:44.496 --> 00:22:50.402
The hot summer passed and the cool autumn arrived.

00:22:50.462 --> 00:22:55.456
The Jamestown settlers had little food to eat.

00:22:55.516 --> 00:22:59.437
Many settlers were ill and weak.

00:22:59.497 --> 00:23:02.357
They needed help.

00:23:02.418 --> 00:23:07.390
When winter arrived, there was no food.

00:23:07.450 --> 00:23:11.631
Pocahontas helped the Jamestown settlers.

00:23:11.691 --> 00:23:17.987
She asked her father for corn, meat, and other food.

00:23:18.047 --> 00:23:26.206
Pocahontas and other Indians brought the food to Jamestown in big baskets.

00:23:26.266 --> 00:23:33.940
The courageous Indian princess helped the settlers to live during the cold winter.

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:38.074
Ships came to Jamestown from England.

00:23:38.134 --> 00:23:42.246
Powhatan was not happy about this.

00:23:42.306 --> 00:23:46.008
More white men came to the new world.

00:23:46.068 --> 00:23:49.074
Powhatan was afraid of them.

00:23:49.134 --> 00:23:52.560
He was afraid of the future.

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:59.454
One winter day, Pohatan sent an Indian messenger to Jamestown.

00:23:59.514 --> 00:24:03.036
He had a message for Captain Smith.

00:24:03.096 --> 00:24:06.858
My chief Pohatan wants to speak to you.

00:24:06.918 --> 00:24:09.020
Follow me.

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:14.564
John Smith followed the messenger to Pohatan's village.

00:24:14.624 --> 00:24:18.297
Pohatan was in his long house.

00:24:18.357 --> 00:24:21.589
John Smith sat next to him.

00:24:21.649 --> 00:24:26.120
We have no more food to give to your people.

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:31.282
You must all leave this land now, said Pohatan.

00:24:31.342 --> 00:24:33.222
Why must we leave?

00:24:33.282 --> 00:24:35.353
asked John Smith.

00:24:35.413 --> 00:24:38.954
The two men talked for a long time.

00:24:39.014 --> 00:24:44.256
At midnight, Pohatan said, It is very late.

00:24:44.316 --> 00:24:48.544
You can sleep in the small cabin near the river.

00:24:48.604 --> 00:24:52.512
Captain Smith accepted the invitation.

00:24:52.572 --> 00:24:56.165
He went to sleep in the small cabin.

00:24:56.226 --> 00:25:01.710
During the night, John Smith heard someone at the door.

00:25:01.770 --> 00:25:06.493
He got up, opened the door, and saw Pocahontas.

00:25:06.554 --> 00:25:09.766
What a surprise to see you, Pocahontas!

00:25:09.826 --> 00:25:11.223
Please come in!

00:25:11.283 --> 00:25:14.880
Oh, Captain Smith, your life is in danger.

00:25:14.940 --> 00:25:19.362
My father and the medicine men want to kill you tonight.

00:25:19.422 --> 00:25:22.512
They don't want white people to stay here.

00:25:22.572 --> 00:25:24.963
You must run away now.

00:25:25.023 --> 00:25:29.014
Dear Princess, you are saving my life again.

00:25:29.074 --> 00:25:31.095
How can I thank you?

00:25:31.155 --> 00:25:32.726
What can I give you?

00:25:32.786 --> 00:25:34.436
Asked Captain Smith.

00:25:34.496 --> 00:25:36.006
Run away now.

00:25:36.067 --> 00:25:37.884
Save yourself.

00:25:37.944 --> 00:25:42.526
Pocahontas touched his hand and ran away.

00:25:42.586 --> 00:25:46.239
John Smith ran out of the cabin.

00:25:46.299 --> 00:25:50.693
He walked to Jamestown in the middle of the night.

00:25:50.753 --> 00:25:58.880
When he arrived in Jamestown, he told the settlers that Pocahontas saved his life again.

00:25:58.940 --> 00:26:04.482
After this adventure, Captain Smith returned to England.

00:26:04.542 --> 00:26:11.084
In Pocahontas' village, everyone thought that Captain Smith was dead.

00:26:11.144 --> 00:26:25.397
Everyone said that he was killed by a gunpowder explosion.

00:26:25.457 --> 00:26:35.667
Couldn't talk.

00:26:35.727 --> 00:26:37.788
Zinsihah Heinrich?

00:26:37.848 --> 00:26:39.688
Yeah, they're spinach.

00:26:39.748 --> 00:26:41.899
My name is Böchner.

00:26:41.959 --> 00:26:43.859
Kiss Böchner.

00:26:43.919 --> 00:26:46.120
Couldn't talk for a Böchner.

00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:49.710
I'll see if you'll come.

00:26:49.770 --> 00:26:52.901
Hello, Rob.

00:26:52.961 --> 00:26:54.372
Hello, Claudia.

00:26:54.432 --> 00:26:55.632
We're good here.

00:26:55.692 --> 00:26:56.332
Thank you.

00:26:56.392 --> 00:27:00.120
Good.

00:27:00.180 --> 00:27:15.303
CHAPTER IV CHIEF POHATON DECLARES WAR More and more white settlers came to Jamestown.

00:27:15.363 --> 00:27:19.574
Jamestown was part of the Virginia colony.

00:27:19.634 --> 00:27:22.656
Chief PoHaton was angry.

00:27:22.716 --> 00:27:26.658
He declared war on the little colony.

00:27:26.718 --> 00:27:29.744
There was a lot of fighting.

00:27:29.804 --> 00:27:34.414
Pocahontas was 17 years old.

00:27:34.474 --> 00:27:39.276
Pohatan wanted to protect his favorite daughter.

00:27:39.336 --> 00:27:43.628
He sent her to live with the Potomac tribe.

00:27:43.688 --> 00:27:48.521
The Potomac Indians were friends of the white people.

00:27:48.581 --> 00:27:52.064
Pocahontas was safe with them.

00:27:52.124 --> 00:27:59.618
Pohatan said to Pocahontas, You must stay with the Potomac Indians.

00:27:59.678 --> 00:28:02.649
You must not go to Jamestown.

00:28:02.709 --> 00:28:05.599
We are at war with Jamestown.

00:28:05.659 --> 00:28:07.350
Yes, Father.

00:28:07.410 --> 00:28:11.251
Pocahontas liked her life with the Potomac's.

00:28:11.311 --> 00:28:16.472
Chief Japazos was the head of the Potomac tribe.

00:28:16.532 --> 00:28:20.379
His wife was Pocahontas' friend.

00:28:20.439 --> 00:28:27.266
Chief Japazos and his wife were friends of Captain Samuel Argoal.

00:28:27.326 --> 00:28:31.177
Captain Argoal was an English explorer.

00:28:31.237 --> 00:28:34.208
He lived in Jamestown.

00:28:34.268 --> 00:28:39.739
One day, Captain Argoal went to visit Chief Japazos.

00:28:39.799 --> 00:28:46.300
When he saw Pocahontas, he said to the chief, Come to see my ship.

00:28:46.360 --> 00:28:49.430
I want to show you a lot of interesting things.

00:28:49.490 --> 00:28:51.539
We can eat on the ship.

00:28:51.599 --> 00:28:53.300
You are very kind.

00:28:53.360 --> 00:28:54.870
Said Pocahontas.

00:28:54.931 --> 00:28:57.482
I want to see an English ship.

00:28:57.542 --> 00:29:02.894
Chief Japazors and his wife wanted to see the ship too.

00:29:02.954 --> 00:29:11.139
Captain Argoel took Pocahontas, Chief Japazors, and his wife to the big sailing ship.

00:29:11.199 --> 00:29:14.100
They looked around the big ship.

00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:18.891
They saw the tall masts and the white sails.

00:29:18.951 --> 00:29:22.040
Then they ate delicious food.

00:29:22.100 --> 00:29:29.202
Pocahontas was very happy and said, Thank you for a wonderful day, Captain Argo.

00:29:29.262 --> 00:29:35.724
At sunset, Chief Japazors and his wife left the ship in a canoe.

00:29:35.784 --> 00:29:38.854
But Pocahontas did not leave.

00:29:38.914 --> 00:29:41.935
She was Captain Argo's prisoner.

00:29:41.996 --> 00:29:43.546
He tricked her.

00:29:43.606 --> 00:29:45.768
Why can't I go with my friends?"

00:29:45.828 --> 00:29:47.638
asked Pocahontas.

00:29:47.698 --> 00:29:51.559
She looked at the canoe and saw her friends.

00:29:51.619 --> 00:29:58.692
Chief Japazor's wife had a new copper kettle and a basket full of colored beads.

00:29:58.752 --> 00:30:05.584
Chief Japazor's and his wife helped Captain Argo capture Pocahontas.

00:30:05.644 --> 00:30:11.025
The copper kettle and the colored beads were their payment.

00:30:11.085 --> 00:30:13.906
Pocahontas cried.

00:30:13.966 --> 00:30:16.690
She had no true friends.

00:30:16.750 --> 00:30:19.261
She asked, what is happening?

00:30:19.322 --> 00:30:21.133
Why am I a prisoner?

00:30:21.193 --> 00:30:26.027
Captain Argle said, I don't want to hurt you Pocahontas.

00:30:26.087 --> 00:30:29.920
I want to take you to Jamestown and keep you there.

00:30:29.980 --> 00:30:36.206
When your father returns the weapons he took from us, I can free you.

00:30:36.226 --> 00:30:38.058
Then you can return home.

00:30:38.118 --> 00:30:40.130
Your father loves you.

00:30:40.190 --> 00:30:42.842
He must return the weapons.

00:30:42.902 --> 00:30:49.634
Pocahontas was a prisoner, but she was not afraid of Captain Argole.

00:30:49.694 --> 00:30:53.165
She was not afraid of the white people.

00:30:53.225 --> 00:30:57.226
Captain Argole took her to Jamestown.

00:30:57.286 --> 00:31:01.067
Everyone in Jamestown liked Pocahontas.

00:31:01.128 --> 00:31:06.519
They remembered that she saved Captain Smith's life twice.

00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:12.724
They also remembered that she brought them food during the long winter.

00:31:12.784 --> 00:31:17.316
Everyone in Jamestown was kind and friendly.

00:31:17.376 --> 00:31:21.348
The women gave her English clothes to wear.

00:31:21.408 --> 00:31:25.530
Pocahontas was a beautiful young woman.

00:31:25.590 --> 00:31:29.472
She learned English manners and customs.

00:31:29.532 --> 00:31:32.487
She made many friends.

00:31:32.547 --> 00:31:39.322
Pocahontas became a Christian, and her Christian name was Rebecca.

00:31:39.382 --> 00:31:43.514
Pohatan did not return the weapons.

00:31:43.574 --> 00:31:47.825
He sent some corn and some broken weapons.

00:31:47.885 --> 00:31:50.436
The war continued.

00:31:50.496 --> 00:31:55.758
Captain Argol was furious because his plan did not work.

00:31:55.818 --> 00:31:59.647
He kept Pocahontas in Jamestown.

00:31:59.707 --> 00:32:04.428
She was his prisoner, but she was not unhappy.

00:32:04.488 --> 00:32:10.604
She liked Jamestown because she learned new things every day.

00:32:10.664 --> 00:32:21.986
My name is Bogna.

00:32:22.046 --> 00:32:33.796
Wouldn't take for a broken up.

00:32:33.856 --> 00:32:38.288
Perhaps it will come.

00:32:38.348 --> 00:32:42.090
Hello, Op.

00:32:42.150 --> 00:32:44.651
Hello, Claudia.

00:32:44.711 --> 00:32:47.002
We're good, dear.

00:32:47.062 --> 00:32:48.182
Thank you.

00:32:48.242 --> 00:32:54.309
Good.

00:32:54.369 --> 00:33:02.188
Indian life.

00:33:02.248 --> 00:33:10.022
The American Indians came from Asia about 40,000 years ago.

00:33:10.082 --> 00:33:16.266
They crossed the Bering Strait and went down to North America.

00:33:16.326 --> 00:33:19.880
These Indians were hunters.

00:33:19.940 --> 00:33:23.132
They hunted wild animals.

00:33:23.192 --> 00:33:28.730
After thousands of years, some Indians became farmers.

00:33:28.790 --> 00:33:31.846
They cultivated corn.

00:33:31.906 --> 00:33:35.267
Other Indians hunted the buffalo.

00:33:35.327 --> 00:33:40.959
They used the buffalo for food, clothing, and tepees.

00:33:41.019 --> 00:33:45.590
American Indians belonged to different tribes.

00:33:45.651 --> 00:33:48.822
Every tribe had a chief.

00:33:48.882 --> 00:33:53.587
There were hundreds of Indian tribes in America.

00:33:53.647 --> 00:33:59.504
The American Indians decorated things with beautiful colors.

00:33:59.564 --> 00:34:02.988
They made masks and decorated them.

00:34:03.048 --> 00:34:07.630
They also made pottery and statues.

00:34:07.690 --> 00:34:12.714
Indians painted pictures on big stone walls.

00:34:12.774 --> 00:34:17.808
These pictures told a story about their life.

00:34:17.868 --> 00:34:23.242
Indians were great hunters and courageous warriors.

00:34:23.302 --> 00:34:25.984
They were strong people.

00:34:26.044 --> 00:34:31.139
They loved and respected nature and animals.

00:34:31.200 --> 00:34:43.460
Different tribes lived in different kinds of homes, the wigwam, the tepee, the longhouse and the pueblo.

00:34:43.520 --> 00:34:49.806
Indians often decorated their tepees with colorful pictures.

00:34:49.866 --> 00:34:58.142
The Indians of the Pacific coast often put big totem poles outside their longhouses.

00:34:58.202 --> 00:35:09.362
Indians used these weapons to hunt and fight, bows and arrows, spears, knives and tomahawks.

00:35:09.422 --> 00:35:25.109
When Captain John Smith came to the New World, some important tribes were the Apaches, the Comanches, the Hurons, the Mohicans, the Navajos, and the Sioux.

00:35:25.169 --> 00:35:29.780
At first the Indians were friendly with the white settlers.

00:35:29.841 --> 00:35:33.342
They taught the settlers how to grow crops.

00:35:33.402 --> 00:35:38.031
They also taught them how to live in the wilderness.

00:35:38.092 --> 00:35:43.652
The white settlers brought the Indians weapons and tools.

00:35:43.712 --> 00:35:48.533
Soon the settlers wanted to take the Indians land.

00:35:48.593 --> 00:35:54.075
Many settlers came to America and they wanted land.

00:35:54.135 --> 00:35:57.986
The Indians didn't want to lose their land.

00:35:58.046 --> 00:36:01.207
The Indian wars began.

00:36:01.267 --> 00:36:03.972
Many people were killed.

00:36:04.033 --> 00:36:10.280
Finally, in the 1890s, the Indian wars ended.

00:36:10.340 --> 00:36:13.552
The Indians lost their land.

00:36:13.612 --> 00:36:18.164
America was now the land of the white settlers.

00:36:18.224 --> 00:36:25.290
Today, American Indians live on reservations.

00:36:25.350 --> 00:36:30.126
What is the difference between the alphabet and the alphabet?

00:36:30.186 --> 00:36:46.170
What is the difference between the alphabet and the alphabet?

00:36:46.230 --> 00:37:32.683
ka, l, m, n, o, p, co, er, s, t, o, fau, v, x, epsilon, That's it.

00:37:32.743 --> 00:37:46.524
Chapter 5 Pocahontas Falls in Love After many months, Pocahontas met John Rolf.

00:37:46.584 --> 00:37:49.986
He was a young tobacco farmer.

00:37:50.046 --> 00:37:53.880
John Rolf was very kind to her.

00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:57.098
She loved him and he loved her.

00:37:57.158 --> 00:38:00.516
They were very happy together.

00:38:00.576 --> 00:38:09.768
John Rolfe wanted to marry Pocahontas, but Pocahontas wanted to speak to her father first.

00:38:09.828 --> 00:38:16.289
One day Pocahontas and John Rolfe went to visit Pohaton.

00:38:16.349 --> 00:38:20.640
The great chief was pleased to see his daughter.

00:38:20.700 --> 00:38:23.851
Father, this is John Rolf.

00:38:23.912 --> 00:38:26.163
I met him in Jamestown.

00:38:26.223 --> 00:38:28.945
He is a very kind person.

00:38:29.005 --> 00:38:32.528
I love him, and I'm going to marry him."

00:38:32.588 --> 00:38:36.540
You are a young woman now, Pocahontas.

00:38:36.600 --> 00:38:40.562
It is time for you to marry the man you love.

00:38:40.622 --> 00:38:44.938
Pohaton embraced his daughter and John.

00:38:44.998 --> 00:38:54.035
Great chief, I love your daughter, and I want to take care of her," said John Rolf.

00:38:54.095 --> 00:39:02.768
In April 1614, Pocahontas married John Rolf in the Anglican Church.

00:39:02.828 --> 00:39:08.416
She was the first American Indian to marry a white man.

00:39:08.476 --> 00:39:12.874
Pocahontas wore a beautiful white dress.

00:39:12.934 --> 00:39:16.168
She had flowers in her hair.

00:39:16.228 --> 00:39:22.452
She and John Rolf laughed and danced on this special day.

00:39:22.513 --> 00:39:27.176
All the people in Jamestown celebrated the marriage.

00:39:27.236 --> 00:39:32.460
There were great festivities with music and dancing.

00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:38.072
Nantakwas and many other Indians came to celebrate.

00:39:38.132 --> 00:39:43.114
At the wedding meal, there were white men and Indians.

00:39:43.174 --> 00:39:46.105
They were all good friends.

00:39:46.166 --> 00:39:49.758
They sat around a long table.

00:39:49.818 --> 00:39:53.940
They were all types of good food to eat.

00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:59.433
Pocahontas' marriage brought peace to the Virginia colony.

00:39:59.494 --> 00:40:02.939
The colony began to grow.

00:40:02.999 --> 00:40:09.567
Soon after their marriage, Pocahontas and John went to London.

00:40:09.628 --> 00:40:15.362
Pocahontas was surprised to see many new things in England.

00:40:15.422 --> 00:40:20.334
In London, she wore beautiful English clothes.

00:40:20.394 --> 00:40:23.466
Everyone wanted to meet her.

00:40:23.526 --> 00:40:27.540
She met the most important people of London.

00:40:27.600 --> 00:40:30.924
She even met King James I.

00:40:30.984 --> 00:40:34.918
Everyone loved the Indian Princess.

00:40:34.978 --> 00:40:41.102
In London, Pocahontas met John Smith again after many years.

00:40:41.162 --> 00:40:44.214
This was a wonderful surprise.

00:40:44.274 --> 00:40:48.316
They talked about their adventures in Jamestown.

00:40:48.377 --> 00:40:52.328
Pocahontas and John Rolfe had a son.

00:40:52.388 --> 00:40:54.779
They were very happy.

00:40:54.840 --> 00:40:57.866
They called him Thomas.

00:40:57.926 --> 00:41:04.044
After Thomas's birth, Pocahontas became very ill.

00:41:04.104 --> 00:41:10.957
She died in England in 1617, at the age of 21.

00:41:11.017 --> 00:41:13.998
This was a tragic event.

00:41:14.058 --> 00:41:16.490
Many people mourned her.

00:41:16.550 --> 00:41:20.772
They remembered the courageous Indian princess.

00:41:20.832 --> 00:41:27.374
Young Thomas was educated in Britain by his uncle, Henry Rolf.

00:41:27.434 --> 00:41:30.654
